  "cash_out_markers": {
    "$comment": "Tokens that make a sentence LITERAL: a named mechanism, a file format, a wire artifact, a measurable quantity. A metaphor is judged 'cashed out' when a sentence in the same paragraph (or, more weakly, the same section) is at least min_sentence_chars long, carries at least min_markers DISTINCT markers from this list, and reaches for no metaphor vehicle of its own. Both floors are hand-tuned: at min_markers=1 and no length floor, 'It is not a database.' scored as a cash-out, which is a negation, not a redemption. Every cash_out verdict in the index is stamped judged=true.",
    "min_markers": 2,
    "min_sentence_chars": 40,
